<title>UK: Amersham lifts Japan JV stake to 50 pct.</title>
<headline>Amersham lifts Japan JV stake to 50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Radioactive healthcare products group Amersham International Plc said on Friday that it has completed moves to raise its stake in its Japanese joint venture Nihon Medi-Physics to 50 percent.</p>
<p>Amersham said in a statement that it had bought additional shares in NMP for a total of 8.28 billion yen.</p>
<p>NMP, which is the dominant player in Japan's radiopharmaceutical market, is now jointly owned by Amerhsam and Sumitomo Chemical Co Ltd.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
